title = AI Gatekeeper settings
intro = Inspect the enforced safety rules and review workflow. Configure an optional local Ollama or Hugging Face model, and add or remove blocking rules for hosts, page text, downloads, and extension popups. Compiled baseline rules and mandatory workflow steps cannot be disabled.
ruleset-version = Ruleset version:
model-review = Local model review:
model-active = Enabled; local service availability is checked for each action.
model-inactive = Not configured; deterministic rules are enforced.
local-model-heading = Optional local model review
local-model-warning = An enabled model receives review data after the mandatory rules. A block, timeout, malformed reply, oversized input, or unavailable local service blocks the action. BlueIce sends data only to the configured credential-free loopback HTTP /v1/ endpoint, with no cloud fallback or API key; the operator controls that local service. Disable the model here if its service is unavailable.
local-model-provider = Provider (ollama or huggingface):
local-model-base = Local API base (for example http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/):
local-model-name = Local model name:
local-model-save = Enable or update local model
local-model-disable = Disable local model review
baseline-rules-heading = Compiled baseline rules
workflow-heading = Required review workflow
category = Category:
conditions = Matching conditions and signatures:
match-logic = Match logic:
applies-at = Applied at workflow steps:
trigger = Trigger:
failure-behavior = If rejected or unavailable:
review-order = Active review order:
compiled-rules-at-step = Compiled rules at this step:
active-additions-at-step = Your active blocking conditions at this step:
addition-host = Host
addition-html-phrase = HTML-text phrase
addition-download-extension = Download extension
addition-popup-phrase = Extension-popup phrase
review-layer-compiled = Compiled deterministic rule base (required)
review-layer-hosts = Your blocked hosts
review-layer-html-phrases = Your blocked HTML-text phrases
review-layer-downloads = Your blocked hosts and/or download extensions
review-layer-popup-phrases = Your blocked extension-popup phrases
review-layer-model = Optional local model (blocks if unavailable)
custom-blocklist-heading = Your additional blocked hosts
mandatory = Mandatory
adjustable = User adjustable
add-host-label = Block host:
add-host-button = Add blocked host
remove-host-button = Remove
custom-blocklist-empty = No additional blocked hosts.
custom-blocklist-match = Applied at URL and download review. A host also blocks its dot-boundary subdomains, ignoring case; a similarly named domain is not blocked. Enter a hostname, not a URL or wildcard.
custom-phrases-heading = Your additional blocked HTML-text phrases
add-phrase-label = Block HTML text:
add-phrase-button = Add blocked phrase
remove-phrase-button = Remove
custom-phrases-empty = No additional blocked phrases.
custom-phrases-match = Applied before page parsing. Phrases match text between HTML tags, including hidden or script text, ignoring case and normalizing whitespace.
custom-extensions-heading = Your additional blocked download extensions
add-extension-label = Block file extension (for example .zip):
add-extension-button = Add blocked extension
remove-extension-button = Remove
custom-extensions-empty = No additional blocked download extensions.
custom-extensions-match = Applied before download bytes begin. File-name suffixes match without case sensitivity.
custom-popup-phrases-heading = Your additional blocked extension-popup phrases
add-popup-phrase-label = Block popup text:
add-popup-phrase-button = Add blocked popup phrase
remove-popup-phrase-button = Remove
custom-popup-phrases-empty = No additional blocked popup phrases.
custom-popup-phrases-match = Applied before an extension's native popup appears. Phrases match the reviewed popup metadata without case sensitivity and with normalized whitespace.
locked-note = Safety floor: every listed baseline rule and workflow step is enforced by the gatekeeper process. Custom blocklists add protection; the separate local model layer is optional.
unavailable = The AI gatekeeper is unavailable, so its settings cannot be read or changed right now.
saved = Gatekeeper settings saved.
invalid = The requested gatekeeper settings change was rejected.
